   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law and the public officers law, in\nrelation to establishing a school speed zone camera demonstration program in\nthe city of Amsterdam; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S10196",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10196-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1180-i, V & T L; amd §87, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10196\n\nSPONSOR: FAHY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law and the public officers law,\nin relation to establishing a school speed zone camera demonstration\nprogram in the city of Amsterdam; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow the city of Amsterdam to establish a school speed school zone\ncamera demonstration program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Vehicle and Traffic Law by adding a new section\n1180-i to authorize the City of Amsterdam to establish a school speed\nzone camera demonstration program with the following provisions:\n\nSubdivision (a): Authorizes the program and permits the installation and\noperation of photo speed violation monitoring systems within no more\nthan five school speeding zones. Establishes applicable time periods\n(school hours, before/after school, and school activities) and requires\nthe City to consider safety-related criteria when selecting locations.\nAlso establishes operational requirements including system testing,\nsignage, operator training, and annual calibration.\n\nSubdivision (b): Establishes owner liability for violations captured by\nthe system when a vehicle exceeds the posted speed limit by more than\nten miles per hour, provided the vehicle was operated with the owner's\npermission.\n\nSubdivision (c): Defines key terms, including \"owner,\" \"photo speed\nviolation monitoring system,\" \"school speed zone.\"\n\nSubdivision (d): Provides that photographic and recorded evidence,\ncertified by a technician, shall constitute prima facie evidence of a\nviolation.\n\nSubdivision (e): Establishes civil penalties, capping fines at fifty\ndollars per violation, with an additional penalty for failure to respond\nto a notice of liability.\n\nSubdivision (f): Clarifies that violations shall not be deemed criminal\nconvictions, shall not be recorded on a driver's record, and shall not\nimpact insurance.\n\nSubdivision (g): Sets forth procedures for issuing a notice of liabil-\nity, including required contents, timelines for mailing, and\ninstructions for contesting violations.\n\nSubdivision (h): Provides that adjudication shall be conducted by the\ncity of Amsterdam parking violations bureau or other authorized agency.\n\nSubdivision (i): Establishes a defense where the vehicle or license\nplates were reported stolen prior to the violation.\n\nSubdivision (j): Provides rules for leased or rented vehicles, allowing\nliability to be transferred to the lessee under specified conditions.\n\nSubdivision (k): Allows an owner to seek indemnification from the opera-\ntor and provides a defense where the vehicle was used without the\nowner's consent.\n\nSubdivision (1): Clarifies that the section does not limit the liability\nof the vehicle operator under other provisions of law.\n\nSubdivision (m): Requires the City of Amsterdam to submit annual reports\ndetailing program performance, including violations, crashes, revenues,\nexpenses, and adjudication outcomes.\n\nSubdivision (n): Establishes a defense where the monitoring system was\nmalfunctioning at the time of the alleged violation.\n\nSection 2 Amends the Public Officers Law to exempt photographs, micro-\nphotographs, videotape or other recorded images prepared under the\nauthority of section 1180-i of the vehicle and traffic law.\n\nSection 3 provides that the purchase or lease of equipment for the\ndemonstration program shall be subject to the provisions 12 of section\n103 of the general municipal law.\n\nSection 4 establishes that the act shall take effect on the thirtieth\nday after it becomes law and shall expire on December 31, 2031.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSpeeding in the city of Amsterdam, combined with a law an already over-\nburdened police department, has created a law enforcement challenge and\nsafety concerns.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law and shall expire December 31, 2031, when upon such date the\nprovisions of this act shall be deemed repealed. Effective immediately,\nthe addition, amendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation neces-\nsary for the implementation of this act on its effective date are\nauthorized to be made and completed on or before such effective date.\n",
